WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.467 --> 00:00:02.834
-Welcome, welcome, welcome
to "The Tonight Show."

00:00:02.834 --> 00:00:04.334
You're here.
You made it.

00:00:04.334 --> 00:00:05.400
[ Cheers and applause ]
You're watching at home.

00:00:05.400 --> 00:00:08.667
Thank you!

00:00:08.667 --> 00:00:12.400
Guys, today is May the 4th.
-Mm.

00:00:12.400 --> 00:00:14.000
[ Cheering ]

00:00:14.000 --> 00:00:16.701
Also known as Star Wars Day...

00:00:16.701 --> 00:00:20.000
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:20.000 --> 00:00:22.801
...as in, "May the fourth
be with you."

00:00:22.801 --> 00:00:23.934
[ Laughter ]

00:00:23.934 --> 00:00:26.334
That's right.
Star Wars Day, or for guys

00:00:26.334 --> 00:00:28.834
in their 30s celebrating it,
Solo de Mayo.

00:00:28.834 --> 00:00:31.334
[ Laughter ]

00:00:31.334 --> 00:00:34.167
-Whoa-oh!
[ Rim shot ]

00:00:34.167 --> 00:00:36.067
Solo.
-Ah.

00:00:36.067 --> 00:00:37.801
But Star Wars Day
is interesting,

00:00:37.801 --> 00:00:39.901
'cause it's the one time of year
when Tinder tries to match you

00:00:39.901 --> 00:00:41.467
with your sister.
You know what I'm saying?

00:00:41.467 --> 00:00:43.667
[ Laughter ]

00:00:43.667 --> 00:00:46.133
You haven't seen the movie?
Don't blame me.

00:00:46.133 --> 00:00:47.801
Blame George Lucas.
I didn't write it.

00:00:47.801 --> 00:00:49.167
[ Laughter ]

00:00:49.167 --> 00:00:51.234
Let's get to some news.
Over in Italy,

00:00:51.234 --> 00:00:53.634
there's a $700 million
super yacht

00:00:53.634 --> 00:00:56.667
that experts think
belongs to Vladimir Putin.

00:00:56.667 --> 00:01:00.067
And right now it's trying
to set sail before it's seized.

00:01:00.067 --> 00:01:02.601
Yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:02.601 --> 00:01:05.133
Turns out escaping on a yacht
is the last square Putin needs

00:01:05.133 --> 00:01:07.067
in the supervillain Bingo.
It's like...

00:01:07.067 --> 00:01:08.667
[ Laughter ]
"Perfect."

00:01:08.667 --> 00:01:11.334
Yeah, Putin's yacht is kind of
like a Carnival cruise.

00:01:11.334 --> 00:01:14.234
The only difference is you get
food poisoning minus the food.

00:01:14.234 --> 00:01:15.801
[ Laughter ]

00:01:15.801 --> 00:01:17.634
"Sorry.
You get food poisoning."

00:01:17.634 --> 00:01:18.868
[ Laughter ]

00:01:18.868 --> 00:01:20.300
But you can tell
it's Putin's yacht

00:01:20.300 --> 00:01:22.133
'cause all the life jackets
have weights in them.

00:01:22.133 --> 00:01:24.868
-Oh, gee.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:24.868 --> 00:01:26.100
-That's the joke.
[ Rim shot ]

00:01:26.100 --> 00:01:27.467
That's the one --
you need one joke,

00:01:27.467 --> 00:01:28.934
that's the joke, you take.
-That's it.

00:01:28.934 --> 00:01:30.100
-That's all you need.
-Just go home, yeah.

00:01:30.100 --> 00:01:31.234
-That's all you need
right there.

00:01:31.234 --> 00:01:33.501
That's the joke, yeah.
That's a good one.

00:01:33.501 --> 00:01:35.334
Meanwhile, I heard --
This is very interesting.

00:01:35.334 --> 00:01:38.167
I heard that the CIA
has started using Instagram

00:01:38.167 --> 00:01:40.801
to help Russians
share state secrets.

00:01:40.801 --> 00:01:42.434
[ Audience "Oohs" ]

00:01:42.434 --> 00:01:44.133
Spies used
to gather intelligence

00:01:44.133 --> 00:01:45.467
through covert missions.

00:01:45.467 --> 00:01:48.100
Now they just talk to each other
through latte foam art.

00:01:48.100 --> 00:01:51.300
[ Laughter ]

00:01:51.300 --> 00:01:53.701
"How do they do that?"

00:01:53.701 --> 00:01:55.767
Speaking of social media,
Twitter just rolled out

00:01:55.767 --> 00:01:57.801
a new feature
called Twitter Circle,

00:01:57.801 --> 00:02:00.200
which lets users share tweets
with a select group

00:02:00.200 --> 00:02:02.534
of up to 150 people.

00:02:02.534 --> 00:02:05.534
That story again,
Twitter invented the group chat.

00:02:05.534 --> 00:02:07.934
[ Laughter ]

00:02:07.934 --> 00:02:09.934
But I like the idea.
Now you can soft launch

00:02:09.934 --> 00:02:11.434
the tweet that gets you fired,
yeah.

00:02:11.434 --> 00:02:15.033
[ Laughter ]

00:02:15.033 --> 00:02:17.033
"No, don't say that."
"Okay."

00:02:17.033 --> 00:02:19.334
Guys, it is
Teacher Appreciation Week.

00:02:19.334 --> 00:02:22.334
Yeah.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:22.334 --> 00:02:27.234
There are so many teachers out
there who deserve our gratitude,

00:02:27.234 --> 00:02:28.567
but there are
also a lot of teachers

00:02:28.567 --> 00:02:29.767
who we tend to overlook,

00:02:29.767 --> 00:02:32.534
and I'd like to pay tribute
to them now.

00:02:32.534 --> 00:02:34.767
♪♪

00:02:34.767 --> 00:02:36.968
Shop teachers.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:36.968 --> 00:02:39.067
This is your week, too.

00:02:39.067 --> 00:02:41.968
Thanks to you, I know
how to build a birdhouse.

00:02:41.968 --> 00:02:44.300
Sure, that hasn't been useful
in my adult life yet,

00:02:44.300 --> 00:02:45.834
but you never know
when somebody's going to ask you

00:02:45.834 --> 00:02:47.701
to build a birdhouse.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:47.701 --> 00:02:49.834
And remember, guys,
you only need one finger

00:02:49.834 --> 00:02:51.167
to say you're number one.

00:02:51.167 --> 00:02:53.701
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:02:53.701 --> 00:02:56.534
P.E. teachers.
You may not get an apple

00:02:56.534 --> 00:02:57.934
on Teacher Appreciation Week,

00:02:57.934 --> 00:03:00.434
but at least everybody at school
knows what your knees look like.

00:03:00.434 --> 00:03:01.767
[ Laughter ]

00:03:01.767 --> 00:03:03.434
So that counts for something.

00:03:03.434 --> 00:03:04.901
Plus, you get
to blow a whistle at work.

00:03:04.901 --> 00:03:09.334
How cool is that?
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:03:09.334 --> 00:03:11.567
And finally,
substitute teachers.

00:03:11.567 --> 00:03:13.400
[ Laughter ]
You guys are the best.

00:03:13.400 --> 00:03:15.467
When you wheel out
that old Toshiba TV

00:03:15.467 --> 00:03:17.234
on the squeaky cart...
[ Laughter ]

00:03:17.234 --> 00:03:20.534
...we all know we're in for the
best day of the school year.

00:03:20.534 --> 00:03:22.801
Because instead of teaching us
about the Roman empire,

00:03:22.801 --> 00:03:24.834
you're gonna nurse your hangover
while we watch

00:03:24.834 --> 00:03:27.634
the first 45 minutes
of "October Sky."

00:03:27.634 --> 00:03:28.968
[ Laughter ]
So kick your feet up

00:03:28.968 --> 00:03:30.467
on your desk,
pull out your phone,

00:03:30.467 --> 00:03:33.133
and play "Fruit Ninja"
while everyone takes a test.

00:03:33.133 --> 00:03:34.200
You've earned it.

00:03:34.200 --> 00:03:35.634
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:35.634 --> 00:03:39.167
To all the teachers out there,
happy Teacher Appreciation Week.

00:03:39.167 --> 00:03:40.801
We appreciate you.

00:03:40.801 --> 00:03:46.734
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:46.734 --> 00:03:48.400
Well, some news from Washington.

00:03:48.400 --> 00:03:50.767
Today at the White House,
President Biden hosted

00:03:50.767 --> 00:03:55.567
Team U.S.A. athletes from both
the summer and winter Olympics.

00:03:55.567 --> 00:03:57.334
[ Cheers and applause ]
Yeah.

00:03:57.334 --> 00:03:59.634
Yeah.
And why not?

00:03:59.634 --> 00:04:01.400
Because after a few more years
of climate change,

00:04:01.400 --> 00:04:02.667
they're gonna be
combined anyway.

00:04:02.667 --> 00:04:06.000
[ Laughter and groans ]

00:04:06.000 --> 00:04:07.300
That's two good --
-Yeah, come on.

00:04:07.300 --> 00:04:08.834
-That's two good jokes
you got there.

00:04:08.834 --> 00:04:09.834
Two for the price of one
tonight.

00:04:09.834 --> 00:04:11.267
-Wow.

00:04:11.267 --> 00:04:13.434
-Some business news --
I saw that TurboTax

00:04:13.434 --> 00:04:17.167
is giving $141 million
back to its customers

00:04:17.167 --> 00:04:19.701
after making them pay
to file their taxes

00:04:19.701 --> 00:04:21.834
when they could have been done
for free.

00:04:21.834 --> 00:04:23.167
[ Audience "Oohs" ]
-What?

00:04:23.167 --> 00:04:25.033
-Right now, TurboTax
is trying to spin it like,

00:04:25.033 --> 00:04:26.901
"See?
We got you a huge refund!"

00:04:26.901 --> 00:04:29.434
[ Laughter ]

00:04:29.434 --> 00:04:31.968
"Got you a lot of money back."
[ Laughter ]

00:04:31.968 --> 00:04:33.701
Listen to this --
due to inflation,

00:04:33.701 --> 00:04:37.667
AT&amp;T has decided to raise prices
on their wireless plans.

00:04:37.667 --> 00:04:39.000
Yeah, when they heard that,
Netflix was like,

00:04:39.000 --> 00:04:40.634
"Yeah, okay,
let's see how that works out."

00:04:40.634 --> 00:04:42.567
[ Laughter ]

00:04:42.567 --> 00:04:44.234
Well, this is going viral.
A man was caught

00:04:44.234 --> 00:04:46.667
on a Ring doorbell camera
confronting his neighbor

00:04:46.667 --> 00:04:49.167
about a loud party
the night before.

00:04:49.167 --> 00:04:50.634
But he wasn't upset
for the reason you'd think.

00:04:50.634 --> 00:04:51.701
Watch this.

00:05:04.834 --> 00:05:08.067
[ Laughter, cheers, applause ]

00:05:08.067 --> 00:05:09.767
-That's right!

00:05:09.767 --> 00:05:13.434
"I want to party too, man."
-"Come on, man."

00:05:13.434 --> 00:05:15.234
-[ Laughs ]

00:05:15.234 --> 00:05:17.334
It got even more awkward
when the person inside said,

00:05:17.334 --> 00:05:18.634
"Okay.
Then, no more parties."

00:05:18.634 --> 00:05:19.968
"Okay."
[ Laughter ]

